@node API
@chapter API
The API reference for @code{dokgen}: 10 modules and 49 exported names,
generated from the source and the docstrings in it.  They are 38
procedures, 3 parameters, 1 record type and 7 variables.  Every module
has a section of its own and every name links to its definition; the
index filters all of them.

@heading How to read this reference
@enumerate 
@item
Every module has a section of its own; open it in the index, or
with the menu button on a phone.
@item
A module section opens with its exported names and a one-line
summary of each.  Follow a name to its definition, where its signature, its
category and the docstring sit together.
@item
A definition can show the code it is written with: open @code{Source} under the docstring to read the form the module holds, coloured like the
Scheme it is.
@item
To find a name across the whole API, press @code{/} and type
in the index filter.
@end enumerate

@heading A generated chapter
This chapter is generated from the source and the docstrings beside it.
To correct a definition, change the source or its docstring and rebuild
