@node dokgen_cli
@section (dokgen cli)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines the command-line interface of the @command{dokgen}
program.  See the @ref{CLI} section for additional information.

The variable @code{spec} is the specification of the interface, a
@code{<configuration>} record as defined by the guile-config library.  It
names the program, states its version, license and author, and declares
the @code{api} subcommand with its @code{sources} argument and its
@code{destination} keyword.  The procedure @code{call} dispatches a
command line to the procedure that carries it out.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_cli_call,call} — Call an appropriate procedure for the given command.


@item
@ref{dokgen_cli_spec,spec} — A record of the type <configuration>.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_cli_call}
@deffn Procedure call command spec
Call an appropriate procedure for the given command.

@strong{command} (list): A list of strings that represent a command-line
instruction passed to the program (see Guile's command-line procedure).

@strong{spec} (Configuration): A @code{<configuration>} record as
defined by the guile-config library, which specifies the command-line
interface of the program.

@strong{Result}: The @var{command} is followed.  If the command is not
recognized, display help information.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_cli_call}
@example 
(define (call command spec)
  "Call an appropriate procedure for the given command.

  @@strong@{command@} (list):
    A list of strings that represent a command-line instruction passed
    to the program (see Guile's command-line procedure).

  @@strong@{spec@} (Configuration):
    A @@code@{<configuration>@} record as defined by the guile-config
    library, which specifies the command-line interface of the program.

  @@strong@{Result@}:
    The @@var@{command@} is followed. If the command is not recognized,
    display help information."
  (let* [(options (getopt-config-auto command spec))
         (sources (option-ref options '(sources)))
         (destination (or (option-ref options 'destination) DEFAULT_DOC_PATH))
         (mermaid-command (or (option-ref options 'mermaid-command)
                              DEFAULT_MERMAID_COMMAND))
         (gnuplot-command (or (option-ref options 'gnuplot-command)
                              DEFAULT_GNUPLOT_COMMAND))]

    (catch 'match-error
      (lambda ()
        (match (full-command options)
          ((_ "api") (api sources destination mermaid-command gnuplot-command))
          ((_ "stats") (stats sources destination))
          ;; A name with no documentation is what `check' exists to find,
          ;; so it is what its exit status has to say.
          ((_ "check") (unless (zero? (check sources)) (exit 1)))))

      (lambda (. args)
        (begin (format #true "ERROR: Command not found: ~a~%~%" command)
               (emit-help options))))))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

