@node dokgen_commands
@section (dokgen commands)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures that are associated to every command
provided by the command-line interface of the @command{dokgen} program.
See the @ref{CLI} and @xref{dokgen_cli,(dokgen cli)} sections for
additional information.

The variable @code{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} is the directory where the API
documentation is saved when the user does not choose one; its value is
@samp{doc/api}.  The documentation is written to a file named
@file{index.texi} inside that directory, and the images of the mermaid
diagrams it holds go in a @file{diagrams} directory beside it.

The procedure @code{api} writes that documentation; @code{check} only
reads, and says which of the exported names are documented nowhere.

@image{diagrams/dokgen_commands-cec3eac2,,,Mermaid diagram}


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_commands_api,api} — Extract the API documentation of the given set of Guile Scheme


@item
@ref{dokgen_commands_check,check} — Report the exported names the modules in SOURCES leave undocumented.


@item
@ref{dokgen_commands_stats,stats} — Measure the tree SOURCES hold and write its statistics chapter.


@item
@ref{dokgen_commands_DEFAULT_DOC_PATH,DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} — A variable.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_api}
@deffn Procedure api sources OPT: destination mermaid-command gnuplot-command
Extract the API documentation of the given set of Guile Scheme modules.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Guile
Scheme modules that compose the code whose API documentation will be
extracted.  These paths can lead to both Scheme files or Scheme
directories.  For example:

@example 
(list «myproject/liby.scm»
      «myproject/liby»
      «myproject/libz.scm»
      «myproject/libz»)
@end example

@strong{destination} (string): Optional path to a directory where the
final Texinfo files will be saved.  If not provided,
@var{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} is used (see the module @ref{dokgen_commands}).
The diagrams the documentation holds are saved to a @file{diagrams}
directory inside it.

@strong{mermaid-command} (string): Optional command that draws a mermaid
diagram, with @code{%i} standing for the diagram's source and @code{%o}
for the path to write its image to.  An empty command draws nothing and
uses the diagrams already in the destination.  With no image the source
is written into the chapter, and the HTML the script presents draws it
in the page.

@strong{gnuplot-command} (string): Optional command that draws a gnuplot
diagram, with @code{%i} standing for the script that sets the output
file and loads the plot and @code{%o} for the path to write its image
to.  An empty command draws nothing and uses the images already in the
destination.

@strong{Result}: The API documentation is saved to the @var{destination}
directory.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_commands_api}
@example 
(define* (api sources
              #:optional (destination DEFAULT_DOC_PATH)
              (mermaid-command diagrams:DEFAULT_MERMAID_COMMAND)
              (gnuplot-command diagrams:DEFAULT_GNUPLOT_COMMAND))
  "Extract the API documentation of the given set of Guile Scheme
   modules.

  @@strong@{sources@} (list of strings):
    Absolute or relative paths to Guile Scheme modules that compose
    the code whose API documentation will be extracted. These paths
    can lead to both Scheme files or Scheme directories. For example:

  @@example
  (list «myproject/liby.scm»
        «myproject/liby»
        «myproject/libz.scm»
        «myproject/libz»)
  @@end example

  @@strong@{destination@} (string):
    Optional path to a directory where the final Texinfo files will be
    saved. If not provided, @@var@{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH@} is used (see the
    module @@ref@{dokgen_commands@}).  The diagrams the documentation holds
    are saved to a @@file@{diagrams@} directory inside it.

  @@strong@{mermaid-command@} (string):
    Optional command that draws a mermaid diagram, with @@code@{%i@} standing
    for the diagram's source and @@code@{%o@} for the path to write its image
    to.  An empty command draws nothing and uses the diagrams already in
    the destination.  With no image the source is written into the
    chapter, and the HTML the script presents draws it in the page.

  @@strong@{gnuplot-command@} (string):
    Optional command that draws a gnuplot diagram, with @@code@{%i@} standing
    for the script that sets the output file and loads the plot and
    @@code@{%o@} for the path to write its image to.  An empty command draws
    nothing and uses the images already in the destination.

  @@strong@{Result@}:
    The API documentation is saved to the @@var@{destination@} directory."
  (let* [(module-names (module-names-of sources))
         (api-file-path (string-append destination
                                       file-name-separator-string
                                       DEFAULT_API_FILE_INDEX))]

    ;; The destination and the renderer are the same for every diagram in
    ;; the run, so they are set once here instead of being passed through
    ;; the templates that write the documentation.
    (parameterize [(diagrams:*diagram-destination* destination)
                   (diagrams:*mermaid-command* mermaid-command)
                   (diagrams:*gnuplot-command* gnuplot-command)]
      (save (stexi->texi
             (stexi:api-chapter
              module-names
              (map stexi:module-section module-names)))
            api-file-path)
      ;; The chapter is readable as it is; these two make it pleasant to
      ;; read in a browser, beside the Texinfo a manual can copy.
      (assets:write-assets! destination))

    (format #true "API documentation saved to ~a~%" destination)))

(defin
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_check}
@deffn Procedure check sources
Report the exported names the modules in SOURCES leave undocumented.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Scheme
files and directories, as for @code{api}.

@strong{Return value} (integer): The number of names reported, so that
the caller decides what an undocumented name means for the exit status.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_commands_check}
@example 
(define (check sources)
  "Report the exported names the modules in SOURCES leave undocumented.

  @@strong@{sources@} (list of strings):
    Absolute or relative paths to Scheme files and directories, as for
    @@code@{api@}.

  @@strong@{Return value@} (integer):
    The number of names reported, so that the caller decides what an
    undocumented name means for the exit status."
  (let [(gap
         (let* [(module-names (module-names-of sources))
                (report (append-map
                         (lambda (module-name)
                           (map (lambda (symbol)
                                  (cons module-name symbol))
                                (data:undocumented-symbols
                                 (resolve-interface module-name))))
                         module-names))]
           (for-each (lambda (entry)
                       (format #true "undocumented: ~a ~a~%"
                               (car entry) (cdr entry)))
                     report)
           (length report)))]
    (if (zero? gap)
        (format #true "dokgen: every exported procedure and macro is documented~%")
        (format #true "dokgen: ~a undocumented name~a~%"
                gap (if (= gap 1) "" "s")))
    gap))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_commands_stats}
@deffn Procedure stats sources OPT: destination
Measure the tree SOURCES hold and write its statistics chapter.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Scheme
files and directories, as for @code{api}.

@strong{destination} (string): Optional path to a directory where the
Texinfo chapter will be saved.  If not provided, @var{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH}
is used.  The chapter is named @file{stats.texi}, so that a manual can
include it beside the API chapter @code{api} writes.

@strong{Result}: The statistics are saved to the @var{destination}
directory, and the numbers a reader of a terminal wants are printed.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_commands_stats}
@example 
(define* (stats sources #:optional (destination DEFAULT_DOC_PATH))
  "Measure the tree SOURCES hold and write its statistics chapter.

  @@strong@{sources@} (list of strings):
    Absolute or relative paths to Scheme files and directories, as for
    @@code@{api@}.

  @@strong@{destination@} (string):
    Optional path to a directory where the Texinfo chapter will be saved.
    If not provided, @@var@{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH@} is used.  The chapter is named
    @@file@{stats.texi@}, so that a manual can include it beside the API
    chapter @@code@{api@} writes.

  @@strong@{Result@}:
    The statistics are saved to the @@var@{destination@} directory, and the
    numbers a reader of a terminal wants are printed."
  (let* [(tree (source-tree sources))
         (parent (first tree))
         (files (second tree))
         (module-names (begin
                         (add-to-load-path parent)
                         (map (lambda (file)
                                (data:file-path->module-name file parent))
                              files)))
         (measured (map (lambda (file)
                          (named (display-name file) (stats:analyze-file file)))
                        files))
         (totals (stats:project-stats measured))
         (coverage (documentation-coverage module-names))
         (history (measured-history (stats:git-stats parent) measured))
         (statistics `((totals . ,totals)
                       (coverage . ,coverage)
                       (modules . ,(length module-names))
                       (git . ,history)))
         (path (string-append destination
                              file-name-separator-string
                              DEFAULT_STATS_FILE_INDEX))]

    (save (stexi->texi (stexi:stats-chapter statistics)) path)
    (assets:write-assets! destination)

    (format #true "~a files, ~a modules, ~a lines of code, ~a decision points~%"
            (length files) (length module-names)
            (assoc-ref totals 'code) (assoc-ref totals 'decisions))
    (format #true "~a of ~a exported names documented~%"
            (car coverage) (cdr coverage))
    (when history
      (format #true "~a commits by ~a author~a, the last on ~a~%"
              (assoc-ref history 'commits)
              (length (assoc-ref history 'authors))
              (if (= 1 (length (assoc-ref history 'authors))) "" "s")
              (assoc-ref history 'last)))
    (format #true "Statistics saved to ~a~%" destination)))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

