@node dokgen_data
@section (dokgen data)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures to retrieve data from Guile Scheme
libraries (e.g.  the names and attributes of their Scheme modules and
the objects these modules export).  This data is then passed to template
procedures to render API documentation in different formats.  See, for
example, the templates used to work with the
@uref{https://www.gnu.org/software/texinfo/,Texinfo format}:
@ref{dokgen_templates_stexi,(dokgen templates stexi)}.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_data_api-symbols,api-symbols} — Return the symbols provided by the interface.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_definition-source,definition-source} — Return the source of NAME as MODULE-NAME defines it, or @code{#false}.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_file-path->module-name,file-path->module-name} — Convert the given Scheme file path into a module name.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_get-file-paths,get-file-paths} — Return a list of paths to Scheme files stored in the directory.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_group-api-objects,group-api-objects} — Return the API objects grouped by kind.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_record-field,record-field} — Get the value of @var{field} from @var{record}.


@item
@ref{dokgen_data_undocumented-symbols,undocumented-symbols} — Return the names @var{interface} exports without documenting them.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_api-symbols}
@deffn Procedure api-symbols interface
Return the symbols provided by the interface.

@strong{interface} (interface): A module's @code{<interface>} record as
returned by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (list of symbols): Where every symbol identifies a
public object exported by the @var{interface}.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_data_api-symbols}
@example 
(define (api-symbols interface)
  "Return the symbols provided by the interface.

  @@strong@{interface@} (interface):
    A module's @@code@{<interface>@} record as returned by Guile's
    procedure @@code@{resolve-interface@}.

  @@strong@{Return value@} (list of symbols):
    Where every symbol identifies a public object exported by the
    @@var@{interface@}."
  (hash-map->list
   (lambda (key var) key)
   (record-field interface 'obarray)))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_definition-source}
@deffn Procedure definition-source module-name name
Return the source of NAME as MODULE-NAME defines it, or @code{#false}.

@strong{module-name} (list of symbols): The module the object belongs
to.  For example: @code{'(mylib amodule)}.

@strong{name} (symbol): The name it is exported under.

@strong{Return value} (string or @code{#false}): The text of the
top-level form that defines @var{name}, exactly as the file writes it,
so that a reader of the documentation sees the code behind a definition
and not a second copy of it.  @code{#false} when no file on the load
path holds the module, and when no form defines the name: a binding a
macro invents has no source of its own.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_data_definition-source}
@example 
(define (definition-source module-name name)
  "Return the source of NAME as MODULE-NAME defines it, or @@code@{#false@}.

  @@strong@{module-name@} (list of symbols):
    The module the object belongs to.  For example:
    @@code@{'(mylib amodule)@}.

  @@strong@{name@} (symbol):
    The name it is exported under.

  @@strong@{Return value@} (string or @@code@{#false@}):
    The text of the top-level form that defines @@var@{name@}, exactly as the
    file writes it, so that a reader of the documentation sees the code
    behind a definition and not a second copy of it.  @@code@{#false@} when no
    file on the load path holds the module, and when no form defines the
    name: a binding a macro invents has no source of its own."
  (and=> (module-file module-name)
         (lambda (file)
           (call-with-input-file file
             (lambda (port)
               (let loop ()
                 (let [(start (ftell port))
                       (form (read port))]
                   (cond
                    [(eof-object? form) #false]
                    [(definition-form? name form)
                     (let* [(end (ftell port))
                            ;; The form starts where `read' met its opening
                            ;; bracket; the comment above it is not shown.
                            (text (begin
                                    (seek port start SEEK_SET)
                                    (get-string-n port (- end start))))
                            (open (or (string-index text #\() 0))]
                       (string-trim-both (substring text open)))]
                    [else (loop)]))))))))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_file-path->module-name}
@deffn Procedure file-path->module-name file-path lib-parent-path
Convert the given Scheme file path into a module name.

@strong{file-path} (string): Absolute path to Guile Scheme module file.
For example: @samp{/home/user/project-x/libx/module-a.scm}.

@strong{lib-parent-path} (string): Absolute path to the directory
containing the library @var{file-path} belongs to.  For example:
@samp{/home/user/project-x/}.

@strong{Return value} (symbol): The name of the module.  For example:
@code{(libx module-a)}.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_data_file-path->module-name}
@example 
(define (file-path->module-name file-path lib-parent-path)
  "Convert the given Scheme file path into a module name.

  @@strong@{file-path@} (string):
    Absolute path to Guile Scheme module file. For example:
    @@samp@{/home/user/project-x/libx/module-a.scm@}.

  @@strong@{lib-parent-path@} (string):
    Absolute path to the directory containing the library
    @@var@{file-path@} belongs to. For example:
    @@samp@{/home/user/project-x/@}.

  @@strong@{Return value@} (symbol):
    The name of the module. For example: @@code@{(libx module-a)@}."
  (let* [(extensionless-file-path (string-drop-right file-path 4))
         (relative-file-path  ; Relative to lib-parent-path.
          (string-drop extensionless-file-path
                       (+ 1 (string-length lib-parent-path))))
         (module-name
          (map
           string->symbol
           (string-split relative-file-path
                         (string->char-set
                          file-name-separator-string))))]

    module-name))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_get-file-paths}
@deffn Procedure get-file-paths directory
Return a list of paths to Scheme files stored in the directory.

Scheme files are identified by their @code{.scm} extension.

@strong{directory} (string): Absolute path to a directory containing a
Guile Scheme library.

@strong{Return value} (list of strings): A list where every element
represents a path to a Scheme file.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_data_get-file-paths}
@example 
(define (get-file-paths directory)
  "Return a list of paths to Scheme files stored in the directory.

  Scheme files are identified by their @@code@{.scm@} extension.

  @@strong@{directory@} (string):
    Absolute path to a directory containing a Guile Scheme library.

  @@strong@{Return value@} (list of strings):
    A list where every element represents a path to a Scheme file."
  (define (enter? name stat result)
    "Return true to enter any directory."
    #true)

  (define (leaf name stat result)
    "Add NAME to RESULT when it has a \".scm\" extension."
    (if (string-suffix? ".scm" name)
	(cons name result)
	result))

  (define (down name stat result)
    "Leave RESULT as it is: directories are not listed."
    result)
  (define (up name stat result)
    "Leave RESULT as it is when leaving a directory."
    result)

  (define (skip name stat result)
    "Leave RESULT as it is for skipped directories."
    result)

  (define (error name stat errno result)
    "Warn about the unreadable NAME and leave RESULT as it is."
    (format (current-error-port) "warning: ~a: ~a~%"
            name (strerror errno))
    result)

  (file-system-fold enter? leaf down up skip error (list) directory))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_group-api-objects}
@deffn Procedure group-api-objects interface
Return the API objects grouped by kind.

A kind can be one of the following: macros, parameters, procedures,
record types, variables.

@strong{interface} (interface): An @code{<interface>} record as returned
by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (alist): Association list where every entry
corresponds to a kind of object and a list of its members.  Only groups
with members are returned.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_data_group-api-objects}
@example 
(define (group-api-objects interface)
  "Return the API objects grouped by kind.

  A kind can be one of the following: macros, parameters, procedures,
  record types, variables.

  @@strong@{interface@} (interface):
    An @@code@{<interface>@} record as returned by Guile's procedure
    @@code@{resolve-interface@}.

  @@strong@{Return value@} (alist):
    Association list where every entry corresponds to a kind of object
    and a list of its members. Only groups with members are returned."
  ;; Helpers.
  (define (add object group catalog)
    "Return a new CATALOG with OBJECT added to the GROUP.

    The groups are compared with @@code@{string=?@} and not with the
    @@code@{eq?@} that @@code@{assq-ref@} would use: two occurrences of the same
    group name need not be the same string once a module is compiled, and a
    catalog that loses its own key is an @@code@{append@} of @@code@{#f@}."
    (map (lambda (entry)
           (if (string=? (car entry) group)
               (cons (car entry) (append (cdr entry) (list object)))
               entry))
         catalog))
  (define (kind-of value)
    "Return the name of the group the API object VALUE belongs to."
    (cond
     [(macro? value) "macros"]
     [(parameter? value) "parameters"]
     [(procedure? value) "procedures"]
     [(record-type? value) "record types"]
     [else "variables"]))
  (define (non-empty-group? group)
    "Return true if the GROUP has members."
    (not (null? (cdr group))))
  (define (symbol-precedes? a b)
    "Return true if symbol A goes before B alphabetically."
    (string<? (symbol->string a) (symbol->string b)))
  ;; Main body.
  (let* [(api-table (record-field interface 'obarray))
         (api-symbols (api-symbols interface))
         (api-symbols-sorted (sort api-symbols symbol-precedes?))
         (api-catalog (list (cons "macros" '())
                            (cons "parameters" '())
                            (cons "procedures" '())
                            (cons "record types" '())
                            (cons "variables" '())))]

    (filter non-empty-group?
     (fold
      (lambda (key result-so-far)
        (let* [(variable (hashq-ref api-table key))
               (value
                (guard
                    (problem [(exception? problem)
                              (raise-exception
                               (make-residual-export-exception
                                "Possible residual export found."
                                key
                                (record-field interface 'name)))])
                    (variable-ref variable)))
               (object (cons key value))]

          (add object (kind-of value) result-so-far)))
      api-catalog
      api-symbols-sorted))))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_record-field}
@deffn Procedure record-field record field
Get the value of @var{field} from @var{record}.

@strong{record} (Guile record or SRFI 9 record): A record of any type.

@strong{field} (symbol): The name of the field.

@strong{Return value} (anything): The value of the field.

If the FIELD does not exist, a @var{no-such-field} exception is raised.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_data_record-field}
@example 
(define (record-field record field)
  "Get the value of @@var@{field@} from @@var@{record@}.

  @@strong@{record@} (Guile record or SRFI 9 record):
    A record of any type.

  @@strong@{field@} (symbol):
    The name of the field.

  @@strong@{Return value@} (anything):
    The value of the field.

  If the FIELD does not exist, a @@var@{no-such-field@} exception is
  raised."
  (let* [(descriptor (record-type-descriptor record))
         (access-field (record-accessor descriptor field))]

    (access-field record)))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_data_undocumented-symbols}
@deffn Procedure undocumented-symbols interface
Return the names @var{interface} exports without documenting them.

@strong{interface} (interface): A module's @code{<interface>} record, as
returned by Guile's procedure @code{resolve-interface}.

@strong{Return value} (list of symbols): The documented gaps of the
module's API, in the order a reader meets them in the manual, so that a
build can fail on them.  An export that is bound to nothing is left out:
that name is a bug in the module and not a gap in its documentation, and
the @code{api} command is where it is reported.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_data_undocumented-symbols}
@example 
(define (undocumented-symbols interface)
  "Return the names @@var@{interface@} exports without documenting them.

  @@strong@{interface@} (interface):
    A module's @@code@{<interface>@} record, as returned by Guile's
    procedure @@code@{resolve-interface@}.

  @@strong@{Return value@} (list of symbols):
    The documented gaps of the module's API, in the order a reader meets
    them in the manual, so that a build can fail on them.  An export that
    is bound to nothing is left out: that name is a bug in the module and
    not a gap in its documentation, and the @@code@{api@} command is where it
    is reported."
  (let [(api-table (record-field interface 'obarray))]
    (sort (filter
           (lambda (symbol)
             (let [(variable (hashq-ref api-table symbol))]
               (and (variable-bound? variable)
                    (undocumented? (variable-ref variable)))))
           (api-symbols interface))
          (lambda (a b) (string<? (symbol->string a) (symbol->string b))))))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

