@node dokgen_writer
@section (dokgen writer)

@c %start of fragment

Procedures for writing data to disk.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Overview
@itemize 
@item
@ref{dokgen_writer_save,save} — Write @var{text} to the file in @var{path}.


@end itemize


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@anchor{dokgen_writer_save}
@deffn Procedure save text path
Write @var{text} to the file in @var{path}.

@strong{text} (string): Arbitrary text.

@strong{path} (string): Absolute or relative path to the file the text
will be written to.

@strong{Result}: If the file doesn't exist, it will be created and the
text will be saved to it.  If the file exists, its contents will be
overwritten.

@anchor{dk_source_dokgen_writer_save}
@example 
(define (save text path)
  "Write @@var@{text@} to the file in @@var@{path@}.

  @@strong@{text@} (string):
    Arbitrary text.

  @@strong@{path@} (string):
    Absolute or relative path to the file the text will be written to.

  @@strong@{Result@}:
    If the file doesn't exist, it will be created and the text will be
    saved to it. If the file exists, its contents will be overwritten."
  (system* "mkdir" "-p" (dirname path))
  (call-with-output-file path
    (lambda (port) (display text port))
    #:encoding "UTF-8"))
@end example

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment
